

# Legendary01 Bookstore Application

## Overview

Legendary01 is a simple, elegant media management system built using Python. It serves as a minimalistic digital bookstore and media library manager, allowing users to add, search, and delete media items such as books, films, and magazines. The application uses a JSON file as its lightweight database and provides a clean, user-friendly graphical interface with Tkinter.

Additionally, a standalone website built with HTML showcases the bookstore project and its features, serving as a portfolio demonstration.



Features

Backend & Data Storage

* Uses a JSON file (`Legendary01_data.json`) to store media items persistently.
* Supports CRUD operations: Add, retrieve, search, and delete media items.
* Each item stores:

  * ID (auto-incremented)
  * Title
  * Creator (Author/Director)
  * Category (Book, Film, Magazine)
  * Year of release/publication
  

Frontend (Tkinter GUI)

* Modern "Midnight & Gold" themed interface for an appealing user experience.
* Sidebar input panel for adding new media entries.
* Main panel displays the list of items in a searchable and sortable table.
* Search functionality with instant filtering by title or creator.
* Delete function to remove selected entries safely with confirmation dialogs.
* Responsive layout with scrollable item list.

Website (HTML)

* Simple HTML website to present the bookstore project.
* Highlights key functionalities and design aspects.
* Acts as a portfolio showcase for the application.

---

## Technical Details

* Programming Language:Python 3.11.1
* GUI Framework:Tkinter with themed styles
* Data Storage:JSON file (`Legendary01.json`)
* HTTP API: Uses `requests` to communicate with backend (assumed Flask or similar running locally at `http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/items`)
* JSON File Management:Safe reading/writing with error handling and data validation.
* User Experience:Clear validation, confirmation dialogs, and error handling to ensure smooth usage.

